{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Hannah, this is normal for a new laptop. Your account has never been set up for Duo, so VPN can't finish signing you in yet. To fix it, we need to set up Duo together, since it needs your phone. Please reply with a time today or tomorrow that works for a short session, remote or in person. Before then, install Duo Mobile from your phone's app store (App Store or Google Play) so it's ready. If you get a Duo approval request before we've set you up, don't approve it, and let us know right away.",
  "internal_note": "Verified sender hannah.lee@brightline.example (user_id 12, Finance, Payroll Specialist, not VIP). Account active, vpn_access true, sign_in_blocked false, failed_login_count 0. check_mfa_status: enrolled false, so Duo was never set up. Laptop BL-LT-0112 (Windows 11) is online, last check-in 2026-10-11 02:44 UTC, disk 50.8% free, no warnings. Per KB-004 'not enrolled' path, next step is a scheduled remote or in-person session with the user present and her phone: install Duo Mobile, install Duo client on laptop if missing, scan activation QR, send and confirm a test push. I have no scheduling tool, so the ticket waits on the user for a time. No password action needed. Once the session is booked, the tech completes enrollment. If she reports pushes she did not request, follow KB-031. Note: the account shows must_change_password true, which is unrelated to Duo but worth checking during the session.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-004",
    "KB-013"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
